==== xc/fonts/bdf/misc/README

The fonts in this directory represent miscellaneous fonts that displays of
all resolutions will probably want to have around:

	fixed width fonts

	DECwindows cursor and session manager fonts

	Sun Open Look glyph fonts

	Kanji and Kana fonts

The Kanji and Kana fonts are as follows:

	k14		kanji 14 pt font
	7x14rk		JIS roman and kana font
	7x14		ASCII fonts with same size for 7x14rk
	8x16rk		JIS roman and kana font
	8x16		ASCII fonts
	12x24rk		JIS roman and kana font
	12x24		ASCII fonts

Roman-kana fonts contain roman part in the left part of them, and kana
in the right. Because of this, kterm (version 3.2.0 or less) can not
display kana characters with these fonts.


Aliases for the Lucida fonts used by XView can be found in ../{75,100}dpi.
They are based on the following "generic" aliases:

